  "model": "Generalist deep-tech firm whose health practice spans therapeutics, diagnostics/medtech and digital health, investing from seed onward with a preference for technically risky, platform-scale bets. It frequently leads or co-leads seed and Series A rounds, and its operating partners sometimes co-found or run portfolio companies (e.g. Liberate Bio, Ukko). Recent therapeutics deals tilt toward AI-enabled chemistry and cell models, in vivo cell therapy and genetic medicine delivery.",
  "summary": "Khosla is an early backer of several category-defining tools and diagnostics companies (Guardant Health, Ultima Genomics, Opentrons, Karius) and has become an increasingly active lead in AI-bio and next-generation therapeutics. Its willingness to write seed checks into unproven platforms makes it a frequent first institutional investor in Bay Area and Boston biotech.",
